# Camoufox WebRTC IP spoofing extensions
#
# Closes the four gaps identified in /Users/lang/.claude/plans/webrtc-canvas-patches-review.md:
#
#   * fe80::/10 link-local IPv6 was treated as "special / never mask" by the
#     existing `isSpecialIP`. fe80 addresses are EUI-64-derived from the host
#     MAC, so they leak hardware identity. This patch moves fe80 to a dedicated
#     `isLinkLocalIPv6` predicate and routes it through `getMaskForIP`, which
#     now fabricates a per-`userContextId`-deterministic link-local replacement.
#
#   * `webrtc:localipv4` / `webrtc:localipv6` (config keys already declared in
#     settings/properties.json but never wired) now feed `WebRTCIPManager`'s
#     local-address slot. RFC1918 candidates are replaced with the configured
#     local address; fall back to the public spoof if the local key is unset.
#
#   * TURN `raddr` field: ALREADY COVERED by the existing line-level
#     `replaceIPAddresses` regex, which matches every IP-shaped substring in
#     each candidate line. No extra regex needed — verified by re-reading
#     PeerConnectionImpl::SpoofCandidateIP.
#
#   * mDNS `xxx.local` host candidates: handled by Phase 5 via the
#     `media.peerconnection.ice.obfuscate_host_addresses` preference toggle —
#     no C++ change here.
#
# Apply after webrtc-ip-spoofing.patch.

